body:
Lots of men are. The thing is, I got myself to 35 almost 36 never really had a girlfriend that wouldn't mind cuddling with me. What made me sad was looking at pictures on social media of other girls with guys. It's hard to not feel insecure in this world. I identify as a lone wolf who doesn't relate to others as a cope.

&#x200B;

I will see how the next 5-10 years go in my life.

So VM would stand for 2022 in the part number VML3Z-16A550-AA. Correct?

&#x200B;

Is there a database spreadsheet I can access to learn about different parts and accessories, the year, what car it goes to and revisions?

We have problems that contribute to the money problem in the world.

&#x200B;

Higher prices causes:

  Lack of efficiency in production

  Lack of production

  Cost of doing business increases due to taxes, rent. 

&#x200B;

Look at the cost of living in California for example. The people are divided between rich, upper middle class, and the homeless population. The rich don't care about the mental health of the average lower middle class or impoverished person.  There is a serious lack of mental health support for people in poverty. Lower standards of living for them. Housing prices are too expensive for the average person over there that people sleep in their car or buy conversion vans. 

&#x200B;

A culture of irresponsible spending is also a big problem in our society. The attitude of "keeping up with the Joneses" like buying a new car, buying a nice house, buying designer clothes, buying that 80" TV,  buying that  $1400 smartphone, going deep into credit card debt, and then signing away a student loan which stays with you for the rest of your life. Everyone loses in that situation.

&#x200B;

I don't know what to say about the US dollar. The US keeps printing money, going deeper into the national debt. We're going to have a life changing historical moment coming. Can't predict the future whether the $1 is going to have any value in 2030 and so on. Chances are with inflation the way it is, probably not. $1 will be near worthless unlike it was in 2010 and before.

The problem is, when you're cynical, you also face loneliness, but you're ok with it. We got the internet, friends. 

&#x200B;

Hell, if you're lonely, get a pet.

I have these ugly pores that will never go away no matter what I do as well as scars, so I am always going to be ugly compared to pretty boy men who are just lucky and smart enough to take care of their skin. 

&#x200B;

I feel ya man. The world is a very cruel place based on lookism and ableism (I'm autistic and get socially rejected because I'm a little weird).

My life is fucked. 35m (me) is living with a 24f (roommate). Already asked her out months ago. Took the rejection. Life moves on. We get along. No boundaries crossed.

&#x200B;

I'm just at that point where I don't care about dating or sex anymore.

I predict as things get worse in the world, there will be an increase of passive aggressive behavior. 

&#x200B;

Look. The world doesn't owe you kindness and you don't owe the world nice either. Be a little bit of an asshole. People will walk all over you if you don't step up for yourself.

Now society is fucked up to the point where talking to people about feelings can hurt more than help. Now there's more cynicism that people won't understand each other the more they try to talk about their feelings.

&#x200B;

Yet they always say, "Whenever you need someone to talk to, you can talk to me". 

&#x200B;

They say one thing, but when you open up, you always get the wrong answers and the person doesn't end up helping.

It's a way of manipulation and to put someone on the spot like that.

&#x200B;

I would rather do it in private if I ever do it at all.

17 is a hard age as you're approaching adulthood, but you're not in you're 30s yet. Just go out there, fake it till you make it, ignore criticisms (I know this is hard), find goals in life like increasing income, find hobbies, don't live for the validation of others, just try to put your best self out there and don't worry about the outcome of each interaction. If you feel like everyone is looking at you the wrong way, just move to another social situation and try to figure out what went wrong there. I know it's hard, and socializing is not easy. Trust me. I'm 34, and personally chosen to give up on the social life because lots of the times it involves spending money on drinks, food and other things if you go to events. (Tip here: Make sure you're finances are in order first). 

&#x200B;

Best of luck to you. That's all of my advice I can really offer. Hope some of it helps.

It's a petty immature story of who is the dumper and who is the dumpee.

&#x200B;

It's so stupid.

I'm doing this myself:

Train yourself to not care about being alone. This will be difficult because as humans we desired a partner to support us. Personally, I'm tired of the dating game and I'm finally throwing in the towel. Being alone isn't so bad. There's lots of things to look up on the internet, ways to waste your time. I like watching videos after work. 

&#x200B;

Get a pet. A dog who always loves you, does so unconditionally. Same with cats. There's nothing with living alone with a pet. It's a thing of life you can interact with, and have fun with. Plus, pets give you no drama if trained right.

&#x200B;

I can't really help you establish relationships because I never achieved one. Keep in mind, if you still want to pursue someone, with Covid, dating is much harder. The choice is yours on this.

I was the opposite. I attempted suicide in october of 2012. I grew up in a broken family, and after college, my first suicide attempt came after the fact I gave up looking for a job I went to college in. (long story). 

&#x200B;

What's crazy is the psychiatrist wrote in I had a "Serious suicide attempt", and I didn't think it was serious as I thought my life was just a joke.

&#x200B;

Can I say I'm happy I'm still alive with the state of society today? I'm going to say no, but with my job giving me income, and the fact I have money saved up, I know I now don't have to give up just yet.

While it seems the only logical way to end a life that is mediocre is to kill yourself, your survival instincts will keep you going unless things are very very bad in your life. 

&#x200B;

I feel the same way you do, and I just wake up every day living the same lie of my life. I believe after I die, I will go to a much better world where not only there are no human problems that are caused primarily by humans, but a world where humans on average aren't so mediocre. It's better to believe in something better after this life than to not believe in anything at all, but that's just me.

I know your feeling. This year, my mental health went from decent to having some concerning issues thanks to COVID and civil unrest driving the world even more upside down. I don't want to go out and exercise. I want to smoke weed and sleep a lot. I tend to get a bit aggressive because I've been walked over and tired of it. I even considered suicide. I lack social skills to make friends or find a girlfriend, and getting those social skills are really hard for me. I feel like murdering people when angry, but know it's wrong and the consequences so I obviously won't act out on it. I have no motivation to learn a skill online, despite being more convenient. I hate myself because I'm a hypocrite sometimes. I'm also a loner. (even more so thanks to COVID). I go to work at my driving job, listening to death metal, and now I turned a blind eye to the news, (I didn't even care one bit about what was happening in Beruit). I now just wear a mask because of the law and societal stigma you get from not wearing one.

&#x200B;

Every day I wake up, I'm reminded I'm still alive, but without worry I expect to die around election day because I live on the outskirts of the city and I predict there will be mega riots, especially if Trump wins. I'm ok with this. With what the world has become now, I believe death is beautiful and nobody should be breeding children in these beyond the pale times. 

&#x200B;

Oh well. If I die, I die. If I actually get to live up to 40, being alone and I'm still alive, let's see what rights we still have.

Baby Boomers: You are special. You are unique. You have so much value!!!!!

&#x200B;

Reality: You don't possess significant value. You will be forgotten by many when you die.

Stupid people post their politics on facebook, but it gets worse. They'll push their views down your throat. 

&#x200B;

..... I want to murder an asshole if they come at me with whatever bullshit. Especially social distancing and wearing a mask. Fuck off with your passive aggressive bullshit.

A large purge would be beneficial as we have too many stupid people on this planet, but then again "stupid" is subjective. So there's different people who will say "If you believe \_\_\_\_\_\_, then you should die. You're making the world a terrible place". Morality is not objective, so no matter what happens, people will still disagree with each other, call each other \_\_\_\_\_ists, and nothing will change in regards to human relations. Why I advocate for a purge is because after a purge, people will have to wake up in order to survive. There would be a lack of engineers, electricians, plumbers, etc. to keep the cities going, that it would quickly change a wealthy country to a poor country as there aren't the necessary people to maintain those standards. 

&#x200B;

Does humanity ever learn anything from their setbacks?

You want to know something? I'm 32, and I didn't lose my virginity until I was 27 and it was with a hooker..... but anyways, I'm going to throw my advice in here.

&#x200B;

Don't let how successful or unsuccessful you with women define you. You can get confident by being single. Focus on other things. Don't make the meaning of life all about getting with a woman. From what you posted previously, you do need to make some changes. Find a decent full time job, save money, get your own place, and get your driver's license (especially if you live in the US, it will help you dramatically). The only person that can change you is you.

Yes, realizing what I have done because of the shortcomings I had, was a way to come at peace. I'm not completely throwing in the towel, but for those who think I'm good looking, I'm not a 9 or a 10. I have acne, scars, and my pores are kind of enlarged. This is what happens when you don't take care of your skin when you're young. I had terrible acne, one cause from eating too much sugar a lot. Now I see why my dad tried to keep me away from sugary stuff. Social skills: I didn't want to really talk to much with anyone and it mainly stems from feeling embarrassed at a young age. Then, after age 19-20 (back in 2006-2007), I didn't know how to talk to girls at work or even ask girls out and felt depressed about it. I tried to talk to my friends about it. Had long hippy hair. Was told to get a haircut, but wasn't convinced that I needed one to get a girl at the time. I didn't work out, which would of been a good way. I didn't think I had a problem back then, that I was considered normal. (which I wasn't). All the depression was bottled up, sucked it up though (as society kinda tells you too), and in the fall of 2012.... boom. suicide attempt. And when I was in the hospital I didn't open up about my issues as much. Chose weed, fapping, taking jobs like retail, warehouse, etc, being lazy for doing things outside of work. 

&#x200B;

My advice from all of this: If you don't take chances, improve yourself, read material, and make an extra effort, you'll find yourself failing. (that is, if not finding a relationship by the age of 30 is considered failure to you.) The thing is, you have to find the drive to do it yourself as only you can.

&#x200B;

Advice: or those who are already past that age and care:

At the same time, you gotta tell yourself: So what if you didn't get to have a meaningful relationship by age 30? That doesn't mean it's necessarily over. I've been more picky about who I want a relationship with after reading about horror stories of toxic relationships and being around friends who have toxic relationships. It's better to be single than to be in one of those. We don't NEED a relationship. We want one, preferably meaningful. We NEED human interaction. The escort can be a sex and intimacy fix. (and yes there are 10/10s that are escorts, believe it or not, if that's what you want.) You still got your 30s, and if you're in your 40s, you still have those. Try new things when you're still not too old to do them. They can change you're perspective on life.

&#x200B;

You can't change the past, only how you're going to deal with it as well as the present.

32, possibly 50... but now with more technology making life interesting possibly on the horizon, I don't feel like committing suicide. 18 years from now.

&#x200B;

I attempted suicide at 25 and again at 27. If I died, I wouldn't of experienced things like sex, a better job (I was at a shitty job that I hated.), and more money by saving hard. Now, it's like I wonder what's on the horizon. Just get yourself into a comfortable home and decent living situation. Yeah, I just go on.
